<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  previsit_intake.v1 — hand-authored operational template (files/12 §1:
  `openehr/previsit_intake.v1.opt`, "hand-authored, committed, sha-pinned").

  WHY THIS FILE IS DELIBERATELY SHALLOW.
  openEHR is a P3 export, not a P0 store (ADR-002 / 00 §3 D8). What P0 owes
  the P3 migration is the archetype-path annotation on every slot (files/05
  §2.1: "keep the archetype-path annotation on every slot: it costs nothing
  and *is* the migration plan"). This template therefore pins exactly two
  things and no more:

    1. the composition and the archetype ROOTS the blueprint names, and
    2. their RM types, so `protocols.bindings.openehr` can assert that every
       declared `openehr_path` resolves with a matching rm_type (files/12
       §8.1; runtime invariant 31).

  It contains NO at-code (`atNNNN`) constraint nodes. Leaf-node binding is
  archetype-internal content that no committed source in this repository
  states, and inventing an at-code would produce a binding table that
  resolves against a fabrication — the failure mode HUMAN_BLOCKERS Rule 1
  exists to prevent. A slot whose leaf path is not yet authored therefore
  carries `openehr_deferred_reason` instead, which the compiler requires and
  files/12 §8 mirrors as a CHECK constraint. Absence is a recorded decision,
  never an oversight.

  ARCHETYPE ID PROVENANCE. The identifier set below is exactly the list
  named in files/03 §7 ("compositions: intake_previsit (CKM archetypes:
  EVALUATION.reason_for_encounter, OBSERVATION.story, OBSERVATION.symptom_sign,
  EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis, ACTION.medication / EVALUATION.adverse_reaction_risk,
  OBSERVATION.phq9 / gad7 ..., EVALUATION.triage_outcome custom)"), written in
  the openEHR `openEHR-EHR-<CLASS>.<concept>.v1` id form. Nothing was added.
  Two consequences are stated rather than left to inference:

    - `COMPOSITION.intake_previsit` and `EVALUATION.triage_outcome` are LOCAL
      archetypes; files/03 §7 marks the latter "custom" and names no CKM
      composition archetype at all.
    - The remaining ids are transcribed from files/03 §7 and have NOT been
      reconciled against a CKM revision here; that reconciliation, and any
      resulting `.vN` bump, belongs to HUMAN_BLOCKERS HB-C12(a).
      Re-authoring in Archetype Designer changes this file's sha256, which
      forces a new questionnaire_definition version and makes the binding
      table diff the review surface (files/12 §8.1).

    - `CLUSTER.provenance` is named in files/03 §7 but is ABSENT here: a
      CLUSTER is not a CONTENT_ITEM, so it cannot sit under `content`, and no
      committed source states which structure hosts it. Adding it would
      require an invented at-code path. Deferred to HB-C12(a).

  SCHEMA CONFORMANCE (INT-257). This file validates against the openEHR OPT
  1.4 schema, ITS-XML tag Release-1.0.2 `components/ALL/Template.xsd`, which
  tests/protocols/test_opt_schema.py runs offline against a vendored,
  digest-pinned copy. That schema makes `occurrences` and `node_id` mandatory
  on every C_OBJECT, `existence` on every C_ATTRIBUTE and `cardinality` on a
  C_MULTIPLE_ATTRIBUTE; the INT-041 file carried none of the last three and
  `occurrences` on the root only, and EHRbase 2.35.1 refused it with HTTP 500
  (INT-032). Every value below is read off a source, none is chosen:

    - root `occurrences` 1..1, both ends included: a template has one root.
      `upper_included` is now explicit — without it the interval [1,1) is
      empty.
    - `content` `existence` 0..1: RM 1.0.2 `COMPOSITION.content` is `0..1`.
    - `content` `cardinality` {0..*; ordered; non-unique}: the RM type is
      `List<CONTENT_ITEM>`, and ADL 1.4 §5.3.4.1 defines a logical list as
      ordered with non-unique membership.
    - each content root `occurrences` 0..* (`upper_included` absent, as an
      unbounded upper requires): how often an entry archetype may sit in
      `content` is stated by the COMPOSITION archetype's content constraint,
      and `openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.intake_previsit.v1` is local and
      unauthored (HB-C12). The entry archetypes state no occurrences for their
      own root. The RM bounds `content` by nothing, and 0..* is that bound
      and nothing tighter; a tighter interval is a modelling decision HB-C12
      owns.
    - every `node_id` is present and EMPTY. A non-empty node id must be a term
      code defined in the terminology the template carries (AOM 1.4
      §4.2.3.1), and this template carries no archetype terminology until
      HB-C12 authors it. EHRbase's OPT parser looks every non-blank node id up
      in that terminology and dereferences the miss, so the archetype root
      code without its term definition is an upload failure, not a nicety;
      the roots are addressed by `archetype_id`, which is what the AQL path
      `/content[<archetype_id>]` names.
-->
<template xmlns="http://schemas.openehr.org/v1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <language>
    <terminology_id>
      <value>ISO_639-1</value>
    </terminology_id>
    <code_string>tr</code_string>
  </language>
  <description>
    <original_author id="organisation">INTAKE</original_author>
    <lifecycle_state>unmanaged</lifecycle_state>
    <details>
      <language>
        <terminology_id>
          <value>ISO_639-1</value>
        </terminology_id>
        <code_string>tr</code_string>
      </language>
      <purpose>Ön görüşme kayıt şablonu — arketip kökü bağlama katmanı.</purpose>
    </details>
  </description>
  <template_id>
    <value>previsit_intake.v1</value>
  </template_id>
  <concept>intake_previsit</concept>
  <definition xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
    <rm_type_name>COMPOSITION</rm_type_name>
    <occurrences>
      <lower_included>true</lower_included>
      <upper_included>true</upper_included>
      <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
      <upper_unbounded>false</upper_unbounded>
      <lower>1</lower>
      <upper>1</upper>
    </occurrences>
    <node_id/>
    <attributes xsi:type="C_MULTIPLE_ATTRIBUTE">
      <rm_attribute_name>content</rm_attribute_name>
      <existence>
        <lower_included>true</lower_included>
        <upper_included>true</upper_included>
        <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
        <upper_unbounded>false</upper_unbounded>
        <lower>0</lower>
        <upper>1</upper>
      </existence>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>EVALUATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.reason_for_encounter.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>OBSERVATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-OBSERVATION.story.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>OBSERVATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-OBSERVATION.symptom_sign.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>EVALUATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.problem_diagnosis.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>ACTION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-ACTION.medication.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>EVALUATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.adverse_reaction_risk.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>OBSERVATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-OBSERVATION.phq9.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>OBSERVATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-OBSERVATION.gad7.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <children xsi:type="C_ARCHETYPE_ROOT">
        <rm_type_name>EVALUATION</rm_type_name>
        <occurrences>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </occurrences>
        <node_id/>
        <archetype_id>
          <value>openEHR-EHR-EVALUATION.triage_outcome.v1</value>
        </archetype_id>
      </children>
      <cardinality>
        <is_ordered>true</is_ordered>
        <is_unique>false</is_unique>
        <interval>
          <lower_included>true</lower_included>
          <lower_unbounded>false</lower_unbounded>
          <upper_unbounded>true</upper_unbounded>
          <lower>0</lower>
        </interval>
      </cardinality>
    </attributes>
    <archetype_id>
      <value>openEHR-EHR-COMPOSITION.intake_previsit.v1</value>
    </archetype_id>
    <template_id>
      <value>previsit_intake.v1</value>
    </template_id>
  </definition>
</template>
